{% comment %}
  Markup copied verbatim from the supplied "collection page.html" (filter bar,
  .filter-box sidebar accordion and the product grid).

  Wired to Shopify natively:
    - sort dropdown  -> collection.sort_options
    - sidebar        -> collection.filters (Search & Discovery app)
    - price slider   -> the price_range filter's min/max params
    - grid           -> paginated collection.products

  Every filter group in the design is rendered from whatever Search & Discovery
  returns - nothing is hard-coded - so adding or reordering a filter in the app
  changes the sidebar with no theme edit. Each group is drawn in one of four
  styles, picked per group (see xd-facet-group):

    price   -> filter.type == 'price_range'            (dual range slider)
    swatch  -> presentation swatch/image, or named in
               "Swatch-style filter groups"            (Colors)
    rating  -> the group named in "Rating tag prefix"   (star rows)
    link    -> named in "Link-style filter groups"      (Category: link rows
                                                        with a count)
    else    -> checkbox list                           (Material, Level,
                                                        Style, Weight)

  Group order, names ("Level" -> "Player Level"), hidden groups and value order
  follow listing.html through section settings - see the loop below.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  MULTI-SELECT, AND WHY THE GROUPS COME FROM TAGS

  Every group is multi-select, in the sense that ticking several values in one
  group returns the union of them. That is not free, and it is the reason the
  sidebar reads tags rather than the metafields this store also has:

    Shopify ORs multiple values of a tag or product-type filter, but
    INTERSECTS multiple values of a list-metafield filter.

  Measured on this store: material Graphite matched 3 products, Carbon Fiber
  matched 2, and both together matched 0 - no paddle is made of both. Ticking a
  second material emptied the grid. Product type behaved the other way round:
  Paddles 2 + Nets 3 = 5. (Repeating a single value returns the same count as
  passing it once, so this is real intersection, not a parsing artefact.)

  So Material, Player Level, Playing Style, Weight and Rating are carried as
  PREFIXED TAGS - "Material: Carbon Fiber", "Level: Advanced" - which arrive as
  a single "Product tags" filter that the loop below slices by prefix into one
  accordion group each. The metafields of the same name are left alone and are
  still correct; the sidebar just does not read them.

  Every value is a checkbox bound to #XdFacetForm, so the form is the one
  source of truth for what is selected: the query string is always
  `new URLSearchParams(new FormData(form))`, never a URL scraped out of the
  markup. Changes are debounced and applied over fetch(), so a shopper can tick
  four materials and two player levels as fast as they can move and the grid is
  fetched once, at the end. The sidebar is never re-rendered mid-session - its
  counts and exhausted states are synced in place from the response - so the
  accordion keeps its scroll position, its open panels, and the drawer stays
  open on a phone.

  The grid keeps the .bestsellers-slider class because main.css hangs the
  bordered card treatment off it (.bestsellers-slider .product-card-image).
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  # Labels typed in the theme editor, normalised for comparison against
  # filter.label. Liquid cannot strip each item of a split, so the separators
  # are normalised before splitting.
  assign link_labels = section.settings.link_style_filters | downcase | replace: ', ', ',' | replace: ' ,', ',' | split: ','
  assign swatch_labels = section.settings.swatch_style_filters | downcase | replace: ', ', ',' | replace: ' ,', ',' | split: ','

  # Colours the design already paints by class in main.css (.color-charcoal
  # etc). Kept as a string because xd-facet-group takes it as one; keep in step
  # with that file if a colour is added there.
  assign design_colours = 'charcoal,navy,crimson,ivory'

  # Active filters.
  #
  # The chip row under the toolbar is shown at every width now that ticking a
  # box no longer reloads the page: on desktop it is the running total of a
  # selection the shopper is still building, and it is the only place a filter
  # from a collapsed accordion panel is visible.
  assign active_count = 0
  for filter in collection.filters
    if filter.type == 'price_range'
      if filter.min_value.value != blank or filter.max_value.value != blank
        assign active_count = active_count | plus: 1
      endif
    else
      assign active_count = active_count | plus: filter.active_values.size
    endif
  endfor

  # "Clear all" drops every filter but must keep the sort order - losing it
  # would silently re-order the grid under the reader.
  assign sort_by = collection.sort_by | default: collection.default_sort_by
  assign clear_url = collection.url
  if sort_by != blank
    assign clear_url = collection.url | append: '?sort_by=' | append: sort_by
  endif
-%}
{%- paginate collection.products by section.settings.products_per_page -%}
  <section class="section-tb-padding96 pt-0">
    <div class="container custom-width">
      {%- comment -%}
        THE FACET FORM IS EMPTY ON PURPOSE.

        It used to wrap the whole section, which put the product grid - and so
        every product card's own add-to-cart <form> - inside it. HTML has no
        nested forms: the parser drops the first inner <form> start tag and
        re-parents its inputs to this one, and the inner `</form>` then closes
        THIS form early. Two things followed, both live before this section was
        touched for mobile:

          * the first card on every page had no <form>, so product-form.js
            threw on it and its BUY NOW did nothing;
          * that card's hidden fields (form_type, product-id, section-id...)
            were serialised into every filter and sort URL.

        So the form is a standalone element and its controls are associated by
        `form="XdFacetForm"` instead - the grid is no longer inside it. Any
        control added to the sidebar needs that attribute or it will not be
        submitted.

        Events do not follow form ownership, only the DOM, so the script at the
        bottom listens on #XdFacets rather than on the form.

        The form still works with JavaScript off: it is a GET form pointed at
        the collection, so the drawer's Apply button (a real submit button)
        navigates to the filtered URL the long way round.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <form id="XdFacetForm" method="get" action="{{ collection.url }}"></form>
      <div
        id="XdFacets"
        data-xd-facets
        data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
        data-collection-url="{{ collection.url }}"
      >
        <div class="row border-bottom g-0 mb-4 xd-facet-bar">
          <div class="col-md-6 d-flex align-items-center gap-4">
            {%- comment -%}
              The mobile control. `.filter-title` beside it is the desktop
              label - a plain caption, not something you can press - so the two
              swap at the drawer's breakpoint rather than one trying to be
              both. `d-lg-none` matters: above 992px the panel is static markup
              and a toggle would still throw Bootstrap's backdrop over it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="xd-filter-toggle d-lg-none heading-font"
              data-bs-toggle="offcanvas"
              data-bs-target="#XdFilterPanel"
              aria-controls="XdFilterPanel"
            >
              <img src="{{ 'filter.svg' | asset_url }}" width="24" height="24" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
              <span>{{ section.settings.filter_label }}</span>
              <span class="xd-filter-toggle__count" data-xd-total-count {% if active_count == 0 %}hidden{% endif %}>
                {{- active_count -}}
              </span>
            </button>
            <div class="filter-title heading-font2 d-none d-lg-flex align-items-center gap-3 heading-font">
              {{ section.settings.filter_label }} <img src="{{ 'filter.svg' | asset_url }}" class="" alt="">
            </div>
            {%- if section.settings.show_sorting -%}
              <div class="sort-box d-flex align-items-center">
                <label class="heading-font heading-font2" for="sortBy">{{ section.settings.sort_label }}</label>
                <select class="form-select heading-font2" name="sort_by" id="sortBy" form="XdFacetForm">
                  {%- for option in collection.sort_options -%}
                    <option value="{{ option.value }}" {% if option.value == sort_by %}selected{% endif %}>
                      {{- option.name | escape -}}
                    </option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          What is currently on, in one scannable row. Each chip clears its own
          value; the last one clears the lot. Shown at every width - see the
          note on active_count above.

          The wrapper is always in the DOM, empty or not, because the AJAX path
          replaces its contents by id.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div id="XdFacetChips" class="xd-active-filters{% if active_count == 0 %} is-empty{% endif %}">
          {%- if active_count > 0 -%}
            {%- for filter in collection.filters -%}
              {%- if filter.type == 'price_range' -%}
                {%- if filter.min_value.value != blank or filter.max_value.value != blank -%}
                  <button type="button" class="xd-active-filters__chip" data-xd-clear-price>
                    {{- filter.min_value.value | default: 0 | money_without_trailing_zeros }}
                    &ndash;
                    {{ filter.max_value.value | default: filter.range_max | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}
                    <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
                  </button>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- for value in filter.active_values -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    A chip unticks the box it stands for rather than following
                    url_to_remove: the checkboxes are the source of truth, and a
                    navigation here would throw away any ticks the shopper has
                    made since the last fetch.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="xd-active-filters__chip"
                    data-xd-uncheck="{{ value.param_name | escape }}"
                    data-xd-uncheck-value="{{ value.value | escape }}"
                  >
                    {{- value.label | escape }}<span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
                  </button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            <a class="xd-active-filters__clear" href="{{ clear_url }}" data-xd-clear-all>
              {{- section.settings.clear_label -}}
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-lg-3">
            {%- comment -%}
              FILTER PANEL

              `.offcanvas-lg` is Bootstrap's responsive variant: a fixed drawer
              below 992px, plain static markup above it - which is the same
              edge the `.col-lg-3` sidebar stacks at.

              The offcanvas classes sit on a wrapper AROUND `.filter-box`, and
              the accordion is deliberately NOT wrapped in `.offcanvas-body`,
              because above 992px Bootstrap gives that element `display: flex`
              and the desktop sidebar would shrink to its content width.

              The panel stays inside the form. Bootstrap only fixes its
              position, it never moves it in the DOM, so every input still
              serialises with #XdFacetForm.

              This subtree is NEVER replaced by the AJAX path - only its counts
              and disabled states are synced - so open panels, scroll position
              and the drawer itself survive a filter change.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div
              class="xd-filter-panel offcanvas-lg offcanvas-start"
              tabindex="-1"
              id="XdFilterPanel"
              aria-labelledby="XdFilterPanelTitle"
            >
              <div class="offcanvas-header">
                <h2 class="xd-filter-panel__title heading-font" id="XdFilterPanelTitle">
                  {{- section.settings.filter_label -}}
                </h2>
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="btn-close"
                  data-bs-dismiss="offcanvas"
                  data-bs-target="#XdFilterPanel"
                  aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}"
                ></button>
              </div>
              <div class="filter-box heading-font2" id="XdFilterBox">
                <div class="accordion accordion-flush" id="filterAccordion">
                {%- comment -%}
                  ONE SHOPIFY FILTER CAN BECOME SEVERAL GROUPS.

                  Material, Player Level, Playing Style, Weight and Rating are
                  carried as prefixed product tags - "Material: Carbon Fiber",
                  "Level: Advanced" - and so arrive as ONE "Product tags" filter
                  whose values are the whole tag. Here that filter is sliced by
                  prefix into a group each, and xd-facet-group strips the prefix
                  off every visible label.

                  They are tags rather than the metafields the store also has,
                  because Shopify INTERSECTS multiple values of a list-metafield
                  filter: measured on this store, material Graphite matches 3
                  and Carbon Fiber matches 2, and both together match 0. Tag
                  values are ORed - Paddles + Nets really does return 5 - which
                  is the only behaviour under which "multi-select" means
                  anything. The metafields are untouched and still correct; the
                  sidebar just does not read them.

                  A tag with no prefix (Pro Series, Tournament, the tags the
                  automatic collections are built on) is not a filter group and
                  is dropped unless "Show unprefixed tags" is on.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- liquid
                  # GROUP ORDER, NAMES AND VISIBILITY
                  #
                  # listing.html runs Prices, Category, Player Level, Playing Style,
                  # Material, Weight, Colors, Rating. Search & Discovery returns its
                  # filters in its own order (Colors before the tag filter), and
                  # the tag groups are named by their prefix ("Level", "Style").
                  # So every group is first described as
                  #
                  #     kind ~ filter index ~ tag prefix ~ display name
                  #
                  # then emitted in "Filter group order". Groups not named there
                  # follow in Shopify's order, so a filter enabled in the app later
                  # still appears with no theme edit; "Hidden filter groups" leaves
                  # out the ones the design has no place for.
                  assign rating_group = section.settings.rating_group | strip
                  assign label_pairs = section.settings.filter_group_labels | split: ','

                  assign hidden_raw = section.settings.hidden_filter_groups | downcase | split: ','
                  assign hidden_blob = ''
                  for hidden_key in hidden_raw
                    assign hidden_clean = hidden_key | strip
                    if hidden_clean != blank
                      assign hidden_blob = hidden_blob | append: hidden_clean | append: '|'
                    endif
                  endfor
                  assign hidden_keys = hidden_blob | split: '|'

                  assign order_raw = section.settings.filter_group_order | downcase | split: ','
                  assign order_blob = ''
                  for order_key in order_raw
                    assign order_clean = order_key | strip
                    if order_clean != blank
                      assign order_blob = order_blob | append: order_clean | append: '|'
                    endif
                  endfor
                  assign order_keys = order_blob | split: '|'

                  assign group_blob = ''
                  for filter in collection.filters
                    assign filter_index = forloop.index0
                    assign is_tag_filter = false
                    if filter.param_name contains 'filter.p.tag'
                      assign is_tag_filter = true
                    endif

                    if is_tag_filter and section.settings.split_tag_filter
                      # Distinct prefixes, in the order the values arrive. A tag
                      # with no prefix (Pro Series, Tournament, the tags the
                      # automatic collections are built on) is not a group.
                      capture prefix_blob
                        for value in filter.values
                          if value.label contains ': '
                            echo value.label | split: ': ' | first
                            echo '|'
                          endif
                        endfor
                      endcapture
                      assign found_prefixes = prefix_blob | split: '|' | uniq
                      for prefix in found_prefixes
                        assign display_name = prefix
                        assign prefix_key = prefix | downcase | strip
                        for pair in label_pairs
                          if pair contains '='
                            assign pair_from = pair | split: '=' | first | downcase | strip
                            if pair_from == prefix_key
                              assign display_name = pair | split: '=' | last | strip
                            endif
                          endif
                        endfor
                        assign group_blob = group_blob | append: 'tag~' | append: filter_index | append: '~' | append: prefix | append: '~' | append: display_name | append: '|'
                      endfor
                      if section.settings.show_unprefixed_tags
                        assign group_blob = group_blob | append: 'untagged~' | append: filter_index | append: '~~' | append: filter.label | append: '|'
                      endif
                    else
                      assign display_name = filter.label
                      assign filter_key = filter.label | downcase | strip
                      for pair in label_pairs
                        if pair contains '='
                          assign pair_from = pair | split: '=' | first | downcase | strip
                          if pair_from == filter_key
                            assign display_name = pair | split: '=' | last | strip
                          endif
                        endif
                      endfor
                      assign group_blob = group_blob | append: 'filter~' | append: filter_index | append: '~~' | append: display_name | append: '|'
                    endif
                  endfor
                  assign all_groups = group_blob | split: '|'

                  assign ordered_blob = ''
                  for order_key in order_keys
                    for group in all_groups
                      assign group_key = group | split: '~' | last | downcase | strip
                      if group_key == order_key
                        assign ordered_blob = ordered_blob | append: group | append: '|'
                      endif
                    endfor
                  endfor
                  for group in all_groups
                    assign group_key = group | split: '~' | last | downcase | strip
                    unless order_keys contains group_key
                      assign ordered_blob = ordered_blob | append: group | append: '|'
                    endunless
                  endfor
                  assign ordered_groups = ordered_blob | split: '|'
                  assign rendered_groups = 0
                -%}

                {%- for group in ordered_groups -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign panel_id = 'facet-' | append: forloop.index
                    assign group_parts = group | split: '~'
                    assign group_kind = group_parts[0]
                    assign filter_index = group_parts[1] | plus: 0

                    # Picked by walking the list and matching the position:
                    # collection.filters[n] with a computed n comes back empty.
                    assign filter = nil
                    for candidate_filter in collection.filters
                      if forloop.index0 == filter_index
                        assign filter = candidate_filter
                      endif
                    endfor
                    assign prefix = group_parts[2] | default: ''
                    assign group_label = group_parts[3]

                    assign group_key = group_label | downcase | strip
                    assign prefix_key = prefix | downcase | strip
                    assign label_key = filter.label | downcase | strip

                    assign is_hidden = false
                    if hidden_keys contains group_key
                      assign is_hidden = true
                    endif
                    if prefix != blank and hidden_keys contains prefix_key
                      assign is_hidden = true
                    endif

                    assign style = 'checkbox'
                    if group_kind == 'tag'
                      if prefix == rating_group
                        assign style = 'rating'
                      elsif swatch_labels contains prefix_key or swatch_labels contains group_key
                        assign style = 'swatch'
                      elsif link_labels contains prefix_key or link_labels contains group_key
                        assign style = 'link'
                      endif
                    elsif group_kind == 'filter'
                      assign presentation = filter.presentation | default: 'text'
                      if filter.type == 'price_range'
                        assign style = 'price'
                      elsif presentation == 'swatch' or presentation == 'image'
                        assign style = 'swatch'
                      elsif swatch_labels contains label_key or swatch_labels contains group_key
                        assign style = 'swatch'
                      elsif filter.param_name contains 'rating'
                        assign style = 'rating'
                      elsif link_labels contains label_key or link_labels contains group_key
                        assign style = 'link'
                      endif
                    endif

                    assign show_count = section.settings.show_counts
                    if style == 'link'
                      assign show_count = true
                    endif

                  -%}
                  {%- unless is_hidden -%}
                    {%- assign rendered_groups = rendered_groups | plus: 1 -%}
                    {%- render 'xd-facet-group',
                      filter: filter,
                      prefix: prefix,
                      group_label: group_label,
                      style: style,
                      panel_id: panel_id,
                      show_count: show_count,
                      rating_suffix: section.settings.rating_suffix,
                      design_colours: design_colours,
                      value_order: section.settings.filter_value_order
                    -%}
                  {%- endunless -%}
                {%- endfor -%}

                {%- if rendered_groups == 0 -%}
                  <div class="accordion-item">
                    <div class="accordion-body ps-3">
                      <p class="filter-link mb-0">{{ section.settings.no_filters_text }}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              </div>
              {%- comment -%}
                The drawer's footer. The grid behind the drawer is already
                updated by the time this is pressed - ticking a box fetches in
                the background at every width - so Apply only has to close the
                drawer and show the shopper the result, with the number of
                matches on the button so nothing has to be taken on trust. It
                stays a real submit button so the form still works with
                JavaScript off; the script cancels the submit and closes the
                drawer instead.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="xd-filter-panel__foot d-lg-none">
                <a class="xd-filter-panel__clear" href="{{ clear_url }}" data-xd-clear-all>
                  {{- section.settings.clear_label -}}
                </a>
                <button type="submit" form="XdFacetForm" class="btn btn-primary xd-filter-panel__apply" data-xd-apply>
                  <span data-xd-apply-label>{{ section.settings.apply_label }}</span>
                  <span data-xd-result-count>({{ collection.products_count }})</span>
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="col-lg-9">
            {%- comment -%}
              Everything the AJAX path replaces lives inside this one element,
              and nothing that holds state does.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div id="XdFacetResults" data-xd-results data-product-count="{{ collection.products_count }}">
              <div class="row g-4 bestsellers-slider">
                {%- for product in collection.products -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    col-6 below 768px. A single full-width card per row turns six
                    products into six screenfuls and gives nothing to compare
                    against; 2-up is the phone product grid everywhere else on
                    this site.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <div class="col-6 col-md-4">
                    {%- render 'xd-product-card',
                      card_uid: forloop.index,
                      product: product,
                      style: 'bestsellers',
                      card_layout: 'listing',
                      buy_label: section.settings.buy_label,
                      on_dark: false,
                      show_rating: section.settings.show_rating
                    -%}
                  </div>
                {%- else -%}
                  <div class="col-12">
                    <p class="filter-link">{{ section.settings.empty_text }}</p>
                  </div>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>

              {%- if paginate.pages > 1 -%}
                <nav class="xd-pager d-flex justify-content-center gap-2 mt-5">
                  {%- if paginate.previous -%}
                    <a class="xd-pager__link" href="{{ paginate.previous.url }}" aria-label="{{ section.settings.prev_label | escape }}">{{ section.settings.prev_label }}</a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- for part in paginate.parts -%}
                    {%- if part.is_link -%}
                      <a class="xd-pager__link" href="{{ part.url }}">{{ part.title }}</a>
                    {%- elsif part.title == paginate.current_page -%}
                      <span class="xd-pager__link is-active" aria-current="page">{{ part.title }}</span>
                    {%- else -%}
                      <span class="xd-pager__link">{{ part.title }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- if paginate.next -%}
                    <a class="xd-pager__link" href="{{ paginate.next.url }}" aria-label="{{ section.settings.next_label | escape }}">{{ section.settings.next_label }}</a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </nav>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endpaginate -%}

<script>
  (function () {
    // The controls live outside the form and are bound to it by their `form`
    // attribute (see the comment on the form above). Events bubble through the
    // DOM, not through form ownership, so they are caught on the wrapper.
    var scope = document.getElementById('XdFacets');
    var form = document.getElementById('XdFacetForm');
    if (!scope || !form) return;

    var sectionId = scope.dataset.sectionId;
    var collectionUrl = scope.dataset.collectionUrl;
    var results = scope.querySelector('[data-xd-results]');
    var chips = document.getElementById('XdFacetChips');
    var filterBox = document.getElementById('XdFilterBox');
    var panel = document.getElementById('XdFilterPanel');

    var lower = scope.querySelector('#lower');
    var upper = scope.querySelector('#upper');
    var minLabel = scope.querySelector('[data-xd-price-min]');
    var maxLabel = scope.querySelector('[data-xd-price-max]');
    var moneyFormat = {{ shop.money_format | json }};
    var localeCode = {{ request.locale.iso_code | json }};

    // Long enough that ticking several boxes in a row is one request, short
    // enough that a single tick still feels immediate.
    var DEBOUNCE = 320;

    var drawer = window.matchMedia('(max-width: 991.98px)');
    var timer = null;
    var inFlight = null;

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
       Price slider
       --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

    // Renders a whole-currency amount through the shop's own money format, so
    // the label matches the server-rendered price everywhere else on the page.
    function money(amount) {
      return moneyFormat.replace(/\{\{\s*\w+\s*\}\}/, function () {
        return amount.toLocaleString(localeCode);
      });
    }

    function syncPriceLabels() {
      if (!lower || !upper) return;
      // Keep the handles from crossing over.
      if (Number(lower.value) > Number(upper.value)) {
        lower.value = upper.value;
      }
      if (minLabel) minLabel.textContent = money(Number(lower.value));
      if (maxLabel) maxLabel.textContent = money(Number(upper.value));
    }

    // The price inputs always carry a value, so left untouched they would pin
    // filter.v.price.gte/lte onto every URL. Disable them (so they are not
    // serialised) whenever they still span the full range.
    function syncPriceInputs() {
      if (!lower || !upper) return;
      var untouched =
        Number(lower.value) <= Number(lower.min) && Number(upper.value) >= Number(upper.max);
      lower.disabled = untouched;
      upper.disabled = untouched;
    }

    function priceIsActive() {
      return Boolean(lower && !lower.disabled);
    }

    function resetPrice() {
      if (!lower || !upper) return;
      lower.value = lower.min;
      upper.value = upper.max;
      syncPriceLabels();
      syncPriceInputs();
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
       The query string
       --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

    // One source of truth: whatever is ticked right now. FormData repeats a
    // name once per checked box, which is exactly the shape Shopify's filter
    // params take for a multi-select group.
    function currentSearch() {
      syncPriceInputs();
      var params = new URLSearchParams();
      new FormData(form).forEach(function (value, key) {
        if (value !== '') params.append(key, value);
      });
      var search = params.toString();
      return search ? '?' + search : '';
    }

    function selectedCount() {
      var total = filterBox
        ? filterBox.querySelectorAll('[data-xd-facet-input]:checked').length
        : 0;
      if (priceIsActive()) total += 1;
      return total;
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
       In-place sidebar sync

       The sidebar is never re-rendered - replacing it would collapse the
       accordion, lose the scroll position and, on a phone, tear the open
       drawer out of the DOM mid-tap. Instead the response's counts and
       exhausted states are copied onto the inputs that are already there,
       keyed by name + value.
       --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /*
      Key for matching a live input against the same value in a fetched
      document. A space will not do as the separator: a tag value is free to
      contain one ("Material: Carbon Fiber"), so name+' '+value could in
      principle be ambiguous. A param name cannot contain a NUL.
    */
    function facetKey(input) {
      return input.name + '\u0000' + input.value;
    }

    // A row's visible state is drawn by the element around its checkbox, not
    // the checkbox itself: the rating rows are labels wrapping a hidden box,
    // the link-style rows an <a> beside one. Called wherever a box changes.
    function syncRow(input) {
      var star = input.closest('.review-star');
      if (star) star.classList.toggle('is-active', input.checked);

      var row = input.closest('.xd-facet-link-row');
      var link = row ? row.querySelector('[data-xd-facet-link]') : null;
      if (link) {
        link.classList.toggle('is-active', input.checked);
        link.classList.toggle('is-disabled', input.disabled);
        link.setAttribute('aria-checked', input.checked ? 'true' : 'false');
        if (input.disabled) link.setAttribute('aria-disabled', 'true');
        else link.removeAttribute('aria-disabled');
      }
    }

    function syncCountsFrom(doc) {
      if (!filterBox || !doc) return;
      var fresh = doc.getElementById('XdFilterBox');
      if (!fresh) return;

      var next = {};
      fresh.querySelectorAll('[data-xd-facet-input]').forEach(function (input) {
        next[facetKey(input)] = {
          count: Number(input.dataset.xdCount || 0),
          disabled: input.disabled,
        };
      });

      filterBox.querySelectorAll('[data-xd-facet-input]').forEach(function (input) {
        var fact = next[facetKey(input)];
        // A value the response no longer lists cannot be reached from here:
        // leave a ticked box alone (it is what produced the result) and grey
        // out an unticked one.
        if (!fact) {
          if (!input.checked) input.disabled = true;
          syncRow(input);
          return;
        }
        input.dataset.xdCount = fact.count;
        // Never disable what the shopper has ticked - that would trap them
        // with no way to untick it.
        input.disabled = input.checked ? false : fact.disabled;
        syncRow(input);

        var row = input.closest('.form-check, .color-option, .review-star, .xd-facet-link-row');
        var text = row ? row.querySelector('[data-xd-count-text]') : null;
        if (text) text.textContent = fact.count;
      });
    }

    // Per-group badges are counted off the live checkboxes, not the response,
    // so they are right on the tap rather than a request later.
    function syncBadges() {
      if (!filterBox) return;
      filterBox.querySelectorAll('[data-xd-group]').forEach(function (group) {
        var badge = group.querySelector('[data-xd-group-count]');
        if (!badge) return;
        var n = group.querySelectorAll('[data-xd-facet-input]:checked').length;
        if (group.querySelector('[data-xd-price]')) n = priceIsActive() ? 1 : 0;
        badge.textContent = n;
        badge.hidden = n === 0;
      });

      var total = scope.querySelector('[data-xd-total-count]');
      if (total) {
        var n = selectedCount();
        total.textContent = n;
        total.hidden = n === 0;
      }
    }

    function syncResultCount(count) {
      var el = scope.querySelector('[data-xd-result-count]');
      if (el && typeof count === 'number' && !isNaN(count)) el.textContent = '(' + count + ')';
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
       Fetch and swap
       --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

    function request(url, push) {
      var target = url + (url.indexOf('?') === -1 ? '?' : '&') + 'section_id=' + sectionId;

      // Only the newest request may write to the DOM. Ticking four boxes
      // faster than the debounce can absorb would otherwise race, and the
      // slowest response - not the last one - would win.
      if (inFlight) inFlight.abort();
      var controller = new AbortController();
      inFlight = controller;

      if (results) results.classList.add('is-loading');
      scope.setAttribute('aria-busy', 'true');

      fetch(target, { signal: controller.signal })
        .then(function (response) {
          if (!response.ok) throw new Error(response.status);
          return response.text();
        })
        .then(function (html) {
          var doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');

          var freshResults = doc.getElementById('XdFacetResults');
          if (freshResults && results) {
            results.innerHTML = freshResults.innerHTML;
            results.dataset.productCount = freshResults.dataset.productCount || '0';
            syncResultCount(Number(freshResults.dataset.productCount));
          }

          var freshChips = doc.getElementById('XdFacetChips');
          if (freshChips && chips) {
            chips.innerHTML = freshChips.innerHTML;
            chips.classList.toggle('is-empty', freshChips.classList.contains('is-empty'));
          }

          syncCountsFrom(doc);
          syncBadges();

          if (push !== false && window.history && window.history.pushState) {
            window.history.pushState({ xdFacets: true }, '', url);
          }
        })
        .catch(function (error) {
          if (error.name === 'AbortError') return;
          // A filtered page the shopper can actually see beats a silent
          // failure: fall back to the navigation this replaced.
          window.location.href = url;
        })
        .finally(function () {
          if (inFlight === controller) {
            inFlight = null;
            if (results) results.classList.remove('is-loading');
            scope.removeAttribute('aria-busy');
          }
        });
    }

    function apply(immediate) {
      // Badges track the checkboxes, so they update on the tap rather than
      // waiting for the response.
      syncBadges();

      var url = collectionUrl + currentSearch();
      if (timer) clearTimeout(timer);
      if (immediate) {
        timer = null;
        request(url, true);
        return;
      }
      timer = setTimeout(function () {
        timer = null;
        request(url, true);
      }, DEBOUNCE);
    }

    function flush() {
      if (!timer) return;
      clearTimeout(timer);
      timer = null;
      request(collectionUrl + currentSearch(), true);
    }

    function closeDrawer() {
      if (!panel || !drawer.matches || !window.bootstrap) return;
      var instance = window.bootstrap.Offcanvas.getInstance(panel);
      if (instance) instance.hide();
    }

    /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
       Events
       --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

    scope.addEventListener('input', function (event) {
      if (event.target.hasAttribute('data-xd-price')) syncPriceLabels();
    });

    scope.addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      var target = event.target;

      if (target.hasAttribute('data-xd-price')) {
        syncPriceLabels();
        // Dragging fires `input` continuously - only the release reaches here,
        // and it still goes through the debounce so moving both handles in one
        // gesture is one request.
        apply(false);
        return;
      }

      if (target.hasAttribute('data-xd-facet-input')) {
        // Rating and link rows style themselves off the element around the
        // checkbox, so their active look has to be driven here, not by CSS.
        syncRow(target);
        apply(false);
        return;
      }

      // Sorting is a deliberate one-off, not something you build up.
      if (target.name === 'sort_by') apply(true);
    });

    scope.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
      // Link-style row (Category): toggle the hidden checkbox it fronts and
      // let the change handler take it from there, like any other box.
      var facetLink = event.target.closest('[data-xd-facet-link]');
      if (facetLink) {
        event.preventDefault();
        var box = document.getElementById(facetLink.getAttribute('data-xd-facet-link'));
        if (!box || box.disabled) return;
        box.checked = !box.checked;
        box.dispatchEvent(new Event('change', { bubbles: true }));
        return;
      }

      // Chip: untick the box it stands for.
      var chip = event.target.closest('[data-xd-uncheck]');
      if (chip) {
        event.preventDefault();
        var name = chip.getAttribute('data-xd-uncheck');
        var value = chip.getAttribute('data-xd-uncheck-value');
        if (filterBox) {
          filterBox.querySelectorAll('[data-xd-facet-input]').forEach(function (input) {
            if (input.name === name && input.value === value) {
              input.checked = false;
              syncRow(input);
            }
          });
        }
        apply(true);
        return;
      }

      if (event.target.closest('[data-xd-clear-price]')) {
        event.preventDefault();
        resetPrice();
        apply(true);
        return;
      }

      var clear = event.target.closest('[data-xd-clear-all]');
      if (clear) {
        event.preventDefault();
        if (filterBox) {
          filterBox.querySelectorAll('[data-xd-facet-input]').forEach(function (input) {
            input.checked = false;
            input.disabled = false;
            syncRow(input);
          });
        }
        resetPrice();
        apply(true);
        closeDrawer();
        return;
      }

      // Pagination stays in the page too, so the shopper does not lose the
      // sidebar's scroll position between pages.
      var pageLink = event.target.closest('.xd-pager__link[href]');
      if (pageLink) {
        event.preventDefault();
        request(pageLink.getAttribute('href'), true);
        if (results) results.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
      }
    });

    // role="checkbox" promises Space toggles it; a link only answers Enter.
    scope.addEventListener('keydown', function (event) {
      if (event.key !== ' ') return;
      var facetLink = event.target.closest('[data-xd-facet-link]');
      if (!facetLink) return;
      event.preventDefault();
      facetLink.click();
    });

    // With JavaScript on, the drawer's Apply button has nothing left to submit
    // - the grid behind it is already current - so it flushes anything still
    // waiting on the debounce and closes the drawer.
    scope.addEventListener('submit', function (event) {
      event.preventDefault();
      flush();
      closeDrawer();
    });

    // Back/forward through the states this script pushed. A reload is the
    // honest answer: the sidebar was mutated in place, so there is no snapshot
    // to restore from.
    window.addEventListener('popstate', function () {
      window.location.reload();
    });

    syncPriceLabels();
    syncPriceInputs();
    syncBadges();
  })();
</script>

